<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/2nd-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Third Macedonian War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">171–168 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Third Macedonian War was fought from 171 to 168 BCE between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perseus-of-macedon">Perseus of Macedon</a>. After early setbacks, the Roman consul <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucius-aemilius-paullus-macedonicus">Lucius Aemilius Paullus</a> crushed the Macedonian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phalanx">phalanx</a> at Pydna in June 168 BCE, and Perseus was taken to Rome. The Antigonid kingdom was abolished and divided into four republics under Roman supervision.</p></div>
